    {
      "title": "Connection Reuse in Development",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Connection Reuse in Development",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why Dev Leaks Connections",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Hot reload== re-runs module code",
                "Each reload makes a new `PrismaClient` and a new ==connection pool==",
                "Symptom: {red:too many connections} error during `next dev`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Save file",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Module re-runs",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New client + pool",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Too many connections",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cache on globalThis",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const globalForPrisma = globalThis as unknown as {",
                " prisma?: PrismaClient }",
                "export const prisma =",
                "  globalForPrisma.prisma ?? new PrismaClient()",
                "if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production')",
                "  globalForPrisma.prisma = prisma"
              ],
              "note": "globalThis survives hot reloads"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Reuse the cached client if it ==exists==",
                "Cache only when `NODE_ENV` is **not** production"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Drizzle",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Driver",
                "globalThis cache?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`postgres`, `pg`",
                  "{red:Yes}, same pattern"
                ],
                [
                  "Serverless over HTTP",
                  "{green:No}, no pool held"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Dev only: `globalThis.prisma ?? new PrismaClient()`. Production loads the module once."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why does next dev exhaust connections?** Every reload builds a new client and pool.",
                "**Why not cache in production?** No hot reload there; the module loads once.",
                "**Does Drizzle need it?** Yes with `pg` or `postgres`; not with HTTP drivers."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Keeping DB Code Server-Only",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Keeping DB Code Server-Only",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Server-Only Guard",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`import 'server-only'` fails the ==build== if a Client Component imports it",
                "Keep queries in a ==data access layer==: `lib/data.ts`",
                "Components import only that file"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "// lib/data.ts",
                "import 'server-only'",
                "export async function getUser(id) {",
                "  const u = await db.user.findUnique({ where: { id } })",
                "  return { id: u.id, name: u.name }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "returns a DTO, not the whole row"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Secrets and DTOs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Value",
                "Reaches browser?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`DATABASE_URL`",
                  "{red:Never}, no prefix"
                ],
                [
                  "Whole DB row",
                  "{red:No}, return a DTO"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A **DTO** holds only the needed fields",
                "Leaving out ==passwordHash== keeps it off the client"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Server Actions",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Server Actions are ==public endpoints==",
                "Re-check ==auth== and authorisation in each one"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never trust the UI: check the session inside every action."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "i18n Routing with [lang] and Dictionaries",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "i18n Routing with [lang] and Dictionaries",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The [lang] Segment",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pages live in ==app/[lang]/==: the locale is a **dynamic segment**",
                "Read it from the `params` prop: `/en/about` gives `lang = 'en'`",
                "Recent Next.js: `params` is a ==Promise==, so **await** it",
                "`generateStaticParams` returns the locales, so each language ==pre-renders=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Middleware Redirect",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Request",
                    "sub": "/about",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Accept-Language",
                    "sub": "read header",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Negotiate",
                    "sub": "supported list",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Redirect",
                    "sub": "/en/about",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Path has no locale: ==redirect== to the negotiated one (default `/en/...`)",
                "Matcher must **exclude** `_next`, static files and `api`: `'/((?!_next|api|.*\\..*).*)'`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Dictionaries",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One ==JSON file per locale==, loaded with dynamic import",
                "Loader wrapped in `server-only`; call it in **Server Components**, pass strings down as props"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "ts",
              "lines": [
                "import 'server-only'",
                "export const getDictionary = (lang) =>",
                "  import(`./${lang}.json`).then(m => m.default)",
                "",
                "export async function generateStaticParams() {",
                "  return [{ lang: 'en' }, { lang: 'fr' }]",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "dictionaries.ts and layout.tsx"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "export default async function Page({ params }) {",
                "  const { lang } = await params",
                "  const t = await getDictionary(lang)",
                "  return <h1>{t.title}</h1>",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Matcher mistake",
              "text": "Without the exclusions, CSS, images and ==/api== calls get redirected to `/en/...` and break."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
